      "spam": false,
      "value": "The old method of sending an invite to a friend in a private world and then they ask the host/owner to send an invite to you is not feasible any longer. We are seeing huge numbers of people in worlds now. Friends instances may as well be public, so a lot of people are going private instances now and finding your friends when logging in is difficult, and sometime impossible. Also there is the issue of room ownership, in the case of a room that has not been made public yet. The maker creates the instance then for what ever reason, they leave, no one else is able to invite people to the room, there is no ownership hand off. It essentially becomes a dead room, with people in it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
